; Leg DX -- the host RECEIVES.  The Victor SENDS TRANS.DAT with --xonxoff.
; START THIS FIRST: the Victor is the initiator.
;
; THE VICTOR OBEYING A REAL XOFF, which no leg in this project has ever
; done.  The host runs "set flow xon/xoff", so its tty sends XOFF when its
; input buffer fills; the Victor's ISR takes it out of the stream, sets
; v9k_txheld, and v9k_ser_put() stops until the XON.
;
; PASS:  byte-exact, stuck=0, cps in leg CC's band.
; READ:  xoff>0 means we obeyed one.  xoff=0 means the host never needed to
;        send one -- a NULL, not a failure, and the leg still shows the
;        interception path did not corrupt anything.
; WATCH: stuck>0 means a hold-off outlasted V9K_FCSPIN (seconds).  With
;        xoff>xon that is a lost XON, which is exactly what tcflow(TCOON)
;        would have recovered if upstream's only call to it were not inside
;        a debug() argument that NODEBUG deletes.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set flow xon/xoff
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16ajDX.pkt
receive gotdx.dat
statistics
